# L §5.14.1's table (round 19, writer 10): `bal(x, d start)` "x's balance before day d's movements (d start, §4.6). On
# the decision's day it reads none of that day's movements, its own result included, so it is no cycle; for d after
# that day it is the decision's future, refused as bal(x, d) is" (LOAD-CYCLE where load sees the day, §8.3,
# RUN-FUTURE otherwise). E3_1_seen_day_cycle_later's save reading bal(konto, start_of(m) start) on
# start_of(m): no cycle; savings' January balance (s1) equals the same balance less floor read on an ask line (chk).
=== m.tally
model r
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source own "own"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place savings: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
input floor: money PLN

move save[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  at start_of(m)
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to savings amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto, start_of(m) start) - floor)

version v
  cite own
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  floor = 100.00 PLN "own"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "statement"
  opening[savings] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "statement"

ask s1: bal(savings, 2026-01-31)
ask chk: bal(konto, 2026-01-01 start) - floor law 2026-01-01
=== expect
chk: 900.00 PLN
  law date 2026-01-01, cut 2026-01-01
s1: 900.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
